  "configuration_id": "config_007",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_017 (scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, transformer, weighted) achieved 0.725 acc, dramatically outperforming config_009 (pca_n2000, same other settings) at 0.586 acc, confirming scvi_n200 as the superior RNA encoder. The current best configuration uses weighted fusion. Question: config_007 is an exact single-variable ablation of config_017, changing only fusion from weighted to concat while keeping scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, transformer aggregation, and multiprofile multimodal identical. This tests whether concatenating modality representations before the head outperforms weighted averaging, a fundamental architectural choice that could unlock further gains. Why this is the best next step: with 7 experiments remaining, establishing the optimal fusion strategy for the proven scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + transformer backbone is the highest-information experiment—it directly extends the strongest evidence we have and will guide all subsequent multiprofile multimodal experiments. Expected cost is similar to config_017 (~3.5-3.7 GPU hours) since the architecture is identical except for the fusion operation."
}

